{
  "dom_id": "question-344038",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "$$\n{y}^{″}+3{\\pi }^{2}y=f(x),\\,y(0)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=0\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above, where $f(x)$ is an odd, $4$-periodic function. Select the missing part in the solution of the IVP, where the second infinite sum on the right-hand side below represents a particular solution of the differential equation.\n\n$$\ny(x)∼{{field-1}}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{12(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{3}(12-{n}^{2})}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [
    {
      "key": "field-1",
      "type": "select",
      "dom_id": "selectList-344038-0",
      "tag": "custom-select",
